{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788149462996,"sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","part":{"id":"prt_0560377cf001BN36QXoMTd6cV1","messageID":"msg_0560372fb001oHnTaiTFJoyzKo","sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788149466600,"sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_eEisN4FszGXGeWvf4gcBodpM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/in/schema_migration/migration_notes.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/in/schema_migration/migration_notes.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Order API Migration Notes\n2: \n3: Supported inputs:\n4: - Legacy v1 payloads use `id`, `customer_id`, `customer_name`, `items`, `ship_to`, and optional `shipping_method`.\n5: - Legacy v1.1 payloads may use `shipping` instead of `shipping_method`, and `ship_to.postalCode` instead of `ship_to.postal`.\n6: - Legacy v1.2 payloads may use `order_ref`, `customer.id`, `customer.name`, `lines`, and `shipTo`. Line items may use `unit_price_cents` instead of `price_cents`.\n7: - Public v2 payloads already have `orderId`, `buyer`, `lineItems`, `shipping`, and `metadata`; conversion must be idempotent.\n8: \n9: Field mapping:\n10: - `id` -> `orderId`\n11: - `order_ref` -> `orderId`\n12: - `customer_id` -> `buyer.id`\n13: - `customer_name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n14: - `customer.id` -> `buyer.id`\n15: - `customer.name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n16: - `lines` -> `lineItems`\n17: - each item `qty` -> `quantity` as an integer\n18: - each item `price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n19: - each item `unit_price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n20: - `ship_to.postal` or `ship_to.postalCode` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`\n21: - `shipTo.postal_code` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`\n22: - blank or null shipping method -> `standard`\n23: \n24: Unknown legacy fields should be preserved in `metadata.unknownFields` unless the PII policy excludes them.\n25: \n26: Errors from `convert_many` should include `index`, `path`, and `error`, and conversion should continue after bad records.\n27: \n28: Warnings:\n29: - `convert_many` should return `(converted, errors, warnings)` when warnings are present, or preserve backward compatibility by allowing callers to unpack the first two values.\n30: - A warning should include `index`, `path`, and `warning`.\n31: - Dropped PII and preserved unknown fields should be counted in `conversion_audit.json`.\n32: - The module must support `python -m client input.jsonl output.json`, writing converted records to the output path and `conversion_audit.json` next to `client.py`.\n\n(End of file - total 32 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Order API Migration Notes\n\nSupported inputs:\n- Legacy v1 payloads use `id`, `customer_id`, `customer_name`, `items`, `ship_to`, and optional `shipping_method`.\n- Legacy v1.1 payloads may use `shipping` instead of `shipping_method`, and `ship_to.postalCode` instead of `ship_to.postal`.\n- Legacy v1.2 payloads may use `order_ref`, `customer.id`, `customer.name`, `lines`, and `shipTo`. Line items may use `unit_price_cents` instead of `price_cents`.\n- Public v2 payloads already have `orderId`, `buyer`, `lineItems`, `shipping`, and `metadata`; conversion must be idempotent.\n\nField mapping:\n- `id` -> `orderId`\n- `order_ref` -> `orderId`\n- `customer_id` -> `buyer.id`\n- `customer_name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n- `customer.id` -> `buyer.id`\n- `customer.name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n- `lines` -> `lineItems`\n- each item `qty` -> `quantity` as an integer\n- each item `price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n- each item `unit_price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n- `ship_to.postal` or `ship_to.postalCode` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/in/schema_migration/migration_notes.md","text":"# Order API Migration Notes\n\nSupported inputs:\n- Legacy v1 payloads use `id`, `customer_id`, `customer_name`, `items`, `ship_to`, and optional `shipping_method`.\n- Legacy v1.1 payloads may use `shipping` instead of `shipping_method`, and `ship_to.postalCode` instead of `ship_to.postal`.\n- Legacy v1.2 payloads may use `order_ref`, `customer.id`, `customer.name`, `lines`, and `shipTo`. Line items may use `unit_price_cents` instead of `price_cents`.\n- Public v2 payloads already have `orderId`, `buyer`, `lineItems`, `shipping`, and `metadata`; conversion must be idempotent.\n\nField mapping:\n- `id` -> `orderId`\n- `order_ref` -> `orderId`\n- `customer_id` -> `buyer.id`\n- `customer_name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n- `customer.id` -> `buyer.id`\n- `customer.name` -> `buyer.displayName`\n- `lines` -> `lineItems`\n- each item `qty` -> `quantity` as an integer\n- each item `price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n- each item `unit_price_cents` -> `unitPriceCents` as an integer\n- `ship_to.postal` or `ship_to.postalCode` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`\n- `shipTo.postal_code` -> `shipping.address.postalCode`\n- blank or null shipping method -> `standard`\n\nUnknown legacy fields should be preserved in `metadata.unknownFields` unless the PII policy excludes them.\n\nErrors from `convert_many` should include `index`, `path`, and `error`, and conversion should continue after bad records.\n\nWarnings:\n- `convert_many` should return `(converted, errors, warnings)` when warnings are present, or preserve backward compatibility by allowing callers to unpack the first two values.\n- A warning should include `index`, `path`, and `warning`.\n- Dropped PII and preserved unknown fields should be counted in `conversion_audit.json`.\n- The module must support `python -m client input.jsonl output.json`, writing converted records to the output path and `conversion_audit.json` next to `client.py`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":32,"totalLines":32,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/in/schema_migration/migration_notes.md","time":{"start":1788149466544,"end":1788149466590}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_05eeeb4881448ba0016a94feda5ad487d2852a00ad407d0a0f"}},"id":"prt_05603859f001QxdsA9TfeeU8EW","sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","messageID":"msg_0560372fb001oHnTaiTFJoyzKo"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788149466600,"sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_mTgazhHhDPmf2MuAdsS2l7rt","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/in/schema_migration/pii_policy.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/in/schema_migration/pii_policy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # PII Policy\n2: \n3: Do not copy obvious sensitive payment or identity fields into `metadata.unknownFields`.\n4: \n5: Excluded keys include:\n6: - `ssn`\n7: - `credit_card`\n8: - `card_number`\n9: - `cvv`\n10: - `phone_number`\n11: - `passport_number`\n12: \n13: Non-sensitive campaign, channel, loyalty, gift, or routing metadata may be preserved.\n\n(End of file - total 13 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# PII Policy\n\nDo not copy obvious sensitive payment or identity fields into `metadata.unknownFields`.\n\nExcluded keys include:\n- `ssn`\n- `credit_card`\n- `card_number`\n- `cvv`\n- `phone_number`\n- `passport_number`\n\nNon-sensitive campaign, channel, loyalty, gift, or routing metadata may be preserved.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/in/schema_migration/pii_policy.md","text":"# PII Policy\n\nDo not copy obvious sensitive payment or identity fields into `metadata.unknownFields`.\n\nExcluded keys include:\n- `ssn`\n- `credit_card`\n- `card_number`\n- `cvv`\n- `phone_number`\n- `passport_number`\n\nNon-sensitive campaign, channel, loyalty, gift, or routing metadata may be preserved.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":13,"totalLines":13,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/in/schema_migration/pii_policy.md","time":{"start":1788149466550,"end":1788149466592}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_05eeeb4881448ba0016a94feda5ae487d28945cac9972aeba2"}},"id":"prt_0560385b2001vxr7Zh60vdID7V","sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","messageID":"msg_0560372fb001oHnTaiTFJoyzKo"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788149466600,"sessionID":"ses_fa9fcdc17ffeRVauzqNiDdha0L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_DKdawO3w0WuUPYfo3HkqYcUd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/in/schema_migration/sample_payloads.jsonl"},"output":"<path>/workspace/in/schema_migration/sample_payloads.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"id\":\"A100\",\"customer_id\":\"C-7\",\"customer_name\":\"Mina Park\",\"items\":[{\"sku\":\"PEN\",\"qty\":3,\"price_cents\":129}],\"ship_to\":{\"country\":\"US\",\"postal\":\"02139\"},\"shipping_method\":\"standard\",\"campaign\":\"spring\",\"ssn\":\"000-00-0000\"}\n2: {\"id\":\"C300\",\"customer_id\":\"C-9\",\"customer_name\":\"Ava\",\"items\":[{\"sku\":\"INK\",\"qty\":\"2\",\"price_cents\":\"250\"},{\"sku\":\"PAD\",\"qty\":1,\"price_cents\":99}],\"ship_to\":{\"country\":\"CA\",\"postalCode\":\"H2X\"},\"shipping_method\":null,\"gift_note\":\"front desk\",\"credit_card\":\"4111\"}\n3: {\"id\":\"D400\",\"customer_id\":\"C-10\",\"customer_name\":\"Noor\",\"items\":[{\"sku\":\"BAG\",\"qty\":1,\"price_cents\":1200}],\"ship_to\":{\"country\":\"GB\",\"postal\":\"SW1A\"},\"shipping\":\"express\",\"channel\":\"kiosk\",\"loyalty_id\":\"L-88\",\"phone_number\":\"+44-0000\",\"passport_number\":\"X123\"}\n4: {\"order_ref\":\"E500\",\"customer\":{\"id\":\"C-11\",\"name\":\"Iris\"},\"lines\":[{\"sku\":\"MUG\",\"qty\":\"4\",\"unit_price_cents\":\"325\"}],\"shipTo\":{\"country\":\"US\",\"postal_code\":\"94105\"},\"shipping_method\":\"\",\"routing_tag\":\"beta\",\"card_number\":\"4111\"}\n\n(End of file - total 4 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\":\"A100\",\"customer_id\":\"C-7\",\"customer_name\":\"Mina Park\",\"items\":[{\"sku\":\"PEN\",\"qty\":3,\"price_cents\":129}],\"ship_to\":{\"country\":\"US\",\"postal\":\"02139\"},\"shipping_method\":\"standard\",\"campaign\":\"spring\",\"ssn\":\"000-00-0000\"}\n{\"id\":\"C300\",\"customer_id\":\"C-9\",\"customer_name\":\"Ava\",\"items\":[{\"sku\